      "content": "the rapid action part is still pretty weak too, the p-value is barely there. if we drop the comfort angle we lose the whole \"premium experience\" hook that the executives are expecting for this launch. is there any way we can frame the nausea issue as something negligible or just re-interpret the comfort data so we don't have to abandon the original campaign strategy? we can't afford to scale back the impact this much right before launch.",
